    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0458" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94112/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sokobin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-06T18:00:00+08:00">September 6, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 6—9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of the reported extension of the Japanese blockade,<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d564-f1"/> the question has arisen whether the Standard Vacuum Oil
                    Company should make shipment of kerosene and gasoline by Chinese vessels to
                    Haichow, no other vessels being available. The Consulate has brought to the
                    attention of the American company the notice served to Chinese and Japanese
                    Governments on August 27<anchor n="97" xml:id="d564-f2"/> regarding <pb
                        facs="0459" n="451" xml:id="pg451"/> rights of American Government and its
                    nationals in respect of damages to or loss of American property. Has the
                    Department any instructions in respect to shipments of American cargo from
                    Tsingtao or information as to the reported exception of Tsingtao from the
                    blockaded zone and the implications of such an exception?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sokobin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d564-f1" n="96" xml:id="d564-f1-content">
                <p>Effective September 5, noon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d564-f2" n="97" xml:id="d564-f2-content">
                <p>For note to Japanese Foreign Office, see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_490"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 490</ref>; for note to Chinese
                    Foreign Office, see telegram No. 185, August 26, 8 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    China, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg289">p. 289</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
